+# Shared GOLD cross-path remediation of Audit 188a3018
+
+Baseline public review commit: `450507815fec44e1c496999e07da1b006861c5dd`.
+Baseline World commit: `7afdd097847d2cd6b5d503734566afc1b78a2c8d`.
+This document belongs to the new local candidate identified by its selected-source manifest. The copied Mint/Python sources have separate exact hashes. It does not identify a new public commit or authorize publication, payment, production migration or deployment.
+
+## Disposition and failure evidence
+
+Finding numbers below refer only to job188a3018, not similarly numbered findings in earlier jobs. `audit6-before-node.log` reproduces nine failing Node cases on the unchanged baseline, including two schema cases for D-03; `audit6-before-python-isolated.log` reproduces both D-04 failures. The earlier Python launcher log records a Windows temporary-directory harness failure and accidental imported-test discovery; it is not counted as defect reproduction. The isolated rerun fixes only the launcher/test import. Expanded Python clock tests also corrected the test clock patcher target before the successful rerun. All attempts are retained privately.
+
+| ID | Original grade | Implementation and preserved boundary | Executable evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| D-01 | Medium | Forward SQL0016 guards every positive `economy_gold_journal` insert before integer addition. Settlement creates immutable config/day/wallet entitlements within the existing page CAS transaction. Its trigger either credits the original journal or keeps a nonspendable owed row. Bounded independent retry credits once when capacity permits. Recovery counts issued and pending entitlements separately and preserves both. Topup/refund credits retain original immutable paid obligations and per-order retry. | `world-gold-audit6.test.mjs` M1; matrix T01–T03; integration exact1025-order reproduction and backup/recovery; native D1 capacity and concurrent retry facts. |
+| D-02 | Low | `sharedServiceAdmission` rejects unlinked catalogue GOLD orders in a shared DB. `createEconomyOrder` refuses new catalogue GOLD admissions there; new services use `goldQuote`. Valid linked payments keep final pause/session/available-balance checks plus atomic debit/paid/challenge/job. Old paid unlinked orders are preserved for read-only inspection, never silently refunded or declared delivered. | Baseline L2; existing pause/challenge/job-fault regressions; current-schema refusal and historical inventory tests. |
+| D-03 | Low | One uncached capability inventory checks112 financial SQL objects and244 columns across37 tables, including required indexes/triggers. All current shared quote/debit/reserve/maintenance paths refuse incomplete schemas with `SCHEMA_INCOMPLETE`. The deployed World POST entry requires readiness even before0014, so no standalone fallback can reopen old money routes. Old paid/refund/held facts remain stored and resume after forward migrations. | Schema version, table/column/index/trigger removal and migration-after-refusal matrix; retained paid pre0015 topup; Worker pre0014 admission and cron diagnostic tests. |
+| D-04 | Low | Python `_identity` separates structural errors from normal identity expiry using one post-response time sample. Expired identity cleanly denies and revokes; trial expiry only removes the trial grant. After balance/network waits the session is checked again and expired rows are revoked. External profile never receives World trial access. | Python audit6 identity/trial now−1/equal/+1, latency, balance wait, malformed upper/type bounds and external-profile cases; prior trial suite retained. |
+| D-05 | Low | A packet is reused only while its original deadline is strictly in the future. At equality, approval refuses `PAID_AUTH_NOT_MINEABLE` while leaving the original hold intact. Expired/latest evidence insufficient for the required reader also stays held. Only original namespace consumption/revocation/strictly-later chain expiry permits terminal settlement. Reuse retains wallet/cost/key/URI/epoch/recipient/domain/run bindings. | Baseline L5; private EVM before/equal/after deadline and pending-proof tests. |
+| D-06 | Low | `encodeGoldResult` validates the persisted JSON against explicit research/fortune review result contracts. Null, blank/empty documents, undefined, cycles, excessive UTF8 or lone surrogates become terminal unusable-result evidence and an original-price refund attempt. Explained zero/false and structured no-signal results are valid; timeout stays unknown. Unbound result contracts refuse new charges and cannot falsely finalize old jobs. Fresh post-validation time preserves lease fencing. | Baseline L6; empty/Unicode/deep JSON, explained zero/no-signal, timeout/idempotency, capacity/refund/reprice and late-lease tests. |
+| D-07 | Low | Both TS and additive SQL mode guard require31337/private-fixture in both directions. Complete original order/wallet/cost/chain/contract/instance/block/outcome proof checks remain. Mode is an internal classification, not proof of public finality. | Baseline L7; direct-SQL wrong-mode and guard-removal calibration, prior full proof/clock checks. |
+| D-08 | Low | Auth must be a nonempty lossless plain JSON object with no functions/symbols/undefined/cycles/accessors/custom serializers/nonfinite values; maximum32 nesting levels and16000 UTF8 bytes. Recorded fixture documents require matching wallet/id (and cost when present); real local wrapped auth/packet/anchor fields are checked against the complete Mint binding. Existing metadata conflicts still return `MINT_ORDER_CONFLICT`; malformed new auth returns `INVALID_MINT_AUTH` with no hold or journal. | Baseline L8; malformed structures, cross-wallet/id, multibyte size, no-write assertions and original same-binding retry tests. Actual private-EVM journey verifies the wrapped format. |
+| D-09 | Info | The private runtime hook receives the validated route and checks the GOLD mint feature for `paid` only. Existing paid holds can still settle while admission is paused. Independent contract-wide emergency pause, eligibility, one-free-per-wallet and supply rules remain. | Baseline I9 plus actual private free Mint with unchanged EMBEO/GOLD and existing paid-hold consumption during paid-only pause. |
+| D-10 | Info/release gates | Documentation/contracts are supplied; real integration is still unverified and disabled. `reviewedEconomyConfig` remains null. No fake provider or fixture finality reader is installed in the deployed entry. | Existing default-entry/HTTP/env capability refusal tests, separate release-gates document. |
+
+The expanded inspection additionally reproduced a stale payment-time sample after asynchronous shared readiness checks (`audit6-cross-path-discovery-before.log`), then corrected it and reran the failure (`...-after.log`). Pending service debit resamples time after admission I/O, checks the original challenge/order deadlines again and uses that fresh time in its SQL authorization predicates. The provider runner similarly supplies a live clock through claim/finalization waits.
+
+## Operation paths and final SQL boundaries
+
+| Operation | Actual trusted entry and data path | Final SQL protection / state |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| UTC staking reward | finalized RPC -> `ingestEconomyEvents` -> bounded `settleEconomy` -> `rewardEntitlementStatement` -> `economy_gold_reward_entitlements` -> original `economy_gold_journal` -> `economy_gold_accounts` | Page CAS + frozen day/position scope; immutable reward identity; capacity predicate before positive addition; owed rows are not book or available GOLD. |
+| Owed reward retry | independent `reconcileWorldGold` -> `reconcileRewardEntitlements` (max32/call) -> original journal + settled marker in one batch | Same wallet/day/config/id/delta/reference; unique original journal; no settled marker without matching journal; per-row cooldown/error and immutable entitlement. |
+| EMBEO topup | `goldQuote` -> immutable product/link/order -> receipt-verifying indexer -> paid evidence -> per-order reconciliation -> `world_gold_entries` | Exact original paid payer/chain/token/treasury/order/amount; authority and capacity triggers; original remaining entitlement only; once-only source reference. |
+| Service payment | `goldQuote` -> existing explicit EOA challenge/signature -> `payEconomyOrderGold` | Complete schema + trusted runtime binding + known result contract + feature control; live session/current wallet/origin; available excludes held; one batch for journal/order/challenge/job. |
+| Legacy catalogue GOLD | retained standalone helpers only on explicit historical DBs; deployed World entry always requires the shared schema | Shared DB refuses unlinked new admissions/challenges/debits. Historical test profile is not a production fallback. No empty-catalogue assumption. |
+| Delivery/retry | trusted `GoldDeliveryProvider` -> max16 `runGoldServiceJobs` -> fenced claim/finish | Provider idempotency key is original orderId; fresh attempt/lease; saved result fetched without another debit; structured failure evidence. Timeout/unknown never authorizes refund. |
+| Refund | terminal failed job -> `refundGold` or original bounded administrator action -> shared credit | Original order/link/cost, failed job, authority/capacity guards, source dedupe; only actual credit permits `refunded`. At capacity job remains failed/refund-pending and original amount remains owed. |
+| Historical correction | offline original and independently rebuilt copies -> `prepare/applyEconomyRecovery` | Event replay entitlement, issued reward/adjustment + separately accounted pending reward; purchases/refunds excluded from earned amounts. Every source snapshot including owed rows is guarded in final atomic plan. New correction that cannot fit is a coded blocked plan, not an automatic partial/forgiven debt. |
+| Paid Mint hold | trusted adapter -> `reserveMintGold` -> mint binding + hold | Full schema, typed metadata/auth, feature check, immutable binding/retry equality, available-balance trigger; no browser-supplied balance/proof. |
+| Mint consume/release | trusted preserved namespace reader -> `settleMintGold` or bounded persisted reconciliation | Complete proof plus bidirectional mode mirror; exact original hold transition; one debit and immutable before/after settlement receipt; wall time/new process/SQLite restore is never release authority. |
+| Administrator | same confirmed owner allowlist + live EOA session -> versioned product/campaign/control or evidenced repair | Atomic before/after and reason/request evidence, immutable quotes and receipts, no arbitrary balance setter. Treasury/pricing trust assumptions remain explicit. |
+
+`economy_gold_days`/`settledDays` now mean that scanning has durably accounted for that day. Outstanding reward rows have a separate uncredited state and bounded retry. World GOLD and staking panes label pending rewards outside spendable balances; the staking heading says “Rewards calculated through.” A failed service is labelled refund-pending, not refunded.
+
+## Compatibility and tests
+
+| DB/profile | New World finances | Maintenance/recovery behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| pre0014 | Deployed World refuses POST finance; shared helpers refuse schema | Original standalone helper tests retain their historic profile; read-only historical recovery remains valid or coded refusal. It is not an alternate deployed money path. |
+|0014 without0015 | `SCHEMA_INCOMPLETE` | No raw missing-table error; paid/refund/held obligations stay stored. |
+|0015 without0016 | `SCHEMA_INCOMPLETE` | Complete shared capability required before resuming. No old migration file is rewritten. |
+| complete0016 | Normal reviewed candidate behavior | Per-order/per-wallet bounded maintenance, refund/reward recovery and original-chain Mint proof. |
+| missing required column/index/trigger/table | `SCHEMA_INCOMPLETE` even when other tables exist | Uncached readiness recognizes restoration/migration on the next call. Inspection reports uninspected rather than a clean inventory. |
+
+Original standalone catalogue tests explicitly run migrations before0014 with all their original authorization, signature, pricing, timing, atomicity and recovery assertions intact. Current shared tests exercise the new refusal/linked-service contracts, page fairness, real private EVM flows and direct SQL. Mutation calibrations issue SQL directly, so an application readiness refusal cannot masquerade as a working SQL guard; removing all relevant proof guards or the particular mode/reserve guard must expose the unsafe transition.
+
+T01–T22 from the supplied supplement are mapped to these tests, earlier retained audit regressions, the actual private-EVM journey and native workerd D1 facts. Final authoritative counts, commands, source pin and hashes are in the sealed candidate validation record after the complete run, not this preliminary document. No local test result is a new Swarm verdict.
